# The BASE graph (fixture 2) — NO quoted triples. Its RDFS / OWL 2 RL closures
# are byte-pinned in expected/base_rdfs_closure.nt / expected/base_owlrl_closure.nt
# and must be UNAFFECTED by the quoted_overlay.ttl quoted triples referring to it.
#
# Derivations (each expected/*.nt line beyond the 9 asserted triples):
#   RDFS  — rdfs2 (domain):      :alice rdf:type :Employee
#           rdfs3 (range):       :acme  rdf:type :Company
#           rdfs7 (subprop):     :alice :affiliatedWith :acme
#           rdfs9 (subclass):    :alice rdf:type :Person
#   OWL RL (additionally)
#         — prp-trp (transitive): :acme :partOf :conglomerate
#           prp-inv (inverse):    :acme :employs :alice
#           inverse schema lift:  :employs rdfs:domain :Company   (= range of :worksFor)
#                                 :employs rdfs:range  :Employee  (= domain of :worksFor)
#           scm-dom1 (subclass):  :worksFor rdfs:domain :Person   (Employee ⊑ Person)
#           scm-rng1 (subclass):  :employs  rdfs:range  :Person   (Employee ⊑ Person)
@prefix : <urn:sparq:qto:> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

:worksFor rdfs:domain :Employee ;
          rdfs:range :Company ;
          rdfs:subPropertyOf :affiliatedWith .
:Employee rdfs:subClassOf :Person .
:partOf a owl:TransitiveProperty .
:employs owl:inverseOf :worksFor .

:alice :worksFor :acme .
:acme :partOf :megacorp .
:megacorp :partOf :conglomerate .
